Package: synthcheck
Title: Tests How Authentic Synthetic Survey Respondents Look
Version: 0.1.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    person("Okan", "Bulut", , "bulut@ualberta.ca", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-5853-1267"))
Description: Tests whether synthetic respondents generated by large language
    models resemble the real survey respondents they are meant to stand in
    for. Overlap shows whether synthetic respondents land where real people
    land, Structure whether the items relate to each other as they do in
    real people, and Behaviour whether synthetic respondents answer the way
    people do (variability, extreme and midpoint answers, acquiescence,
    consistency and person fit). Each index is anchored between a shuffled
    baseline and a second sample of real people, and the synthetic
    authenticity benchmark compares several models in one table. Includes
    real and synthetic responses to the IPIP-HEXACO personality inventory,
    and a 'shiny' app that generates synthetic respondents with 'Anthropic',
    'OpenAI' or local 'Ollama' models and benchmarks them.
